    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a high-ceiling lineup led by **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (84.88) and **Gunnar Henderson** (81.76). **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** is our clear anchor; despite facing a lefty in Kay, his favorable park adjustment and strong SP skill advantage make him the most efficient offensive weapon in our stable. Similarly, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a massive 14% platoon boost against Lambert, ensuring he remains a cornerstone play despite the rotation of the lineup. **Jackson Merrill** (75.10) also secures a premium spot, leveraging a solid matchup against Lugo to keep our stolen base floor secure, as his elite sprint speed remains a pivotal component of our 5x5 strategy. **Drake Baldwin** rounds out our top-tier plays with a 71.33 score, benefiting significantly from his spot at the top of the order, though his status is tempered by a lingering 32% rain risk in his matchup against Quantrill.\n\nRegarding roster construction, the decision to bench **Coby Mayo** (45.99) was our most difficult pivot. **Coby Mayo** landed just shy of the threshold to displace our lower-scoring infielders, primarily due to a projected #7 batting order slot that depressed his run-scoring potential compared to the high-OBP reliability of **Nasim Nunez** or **Curtis Mead**. While **Heliot Ramos** (43.07) and **Josh Jung** (42.86) remain on the outside looking in, the optimizer prioritized the guaranteed platoon edges afforded to players like **Dominic Smith** (59.86), whose specific matchup against Quantrill presents a higher efficiency floor. We remain vigilant on the status of **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, **Nasim Nunez**, **Gunnar Henderson**, **Jacob Wilson**, **Curtis Mead**, **Jackson Merrill**, and **Heliot Ramos**; as their lineups are currently \"Pending,\" any downward shift in their projected batting order could trigger a mid-day reassessment of our efficiency scores.",
